---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = "Privacy | The Web3 Family";
const description = "What this site collects, and why.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
<!-- PRIVACY -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="article-date">Last updated: November 2026</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>This page covers what this site collects, and why, in plain language.</p>
      <p><strong>Microsoft Clarity.</strong> I use Clarity to watch how the site gets used: session recordings and heatmaps, so I can see where a page is confusing. It sets its own cookies to do this.</p>
      <p><strong>Google Analytics.</strong> I use Google Analytics for overall visit counts: how many people land on a page, and where they came from. It also sets its own cookies.</p>
      <p><strong>Analytics and session recordings.</strong> I use PostHog to understand how people use this site, such as which pages they visit, what they click, and, with your permission, anonymous recordings of how they move through a page. Typed form entries are hidden in recordings. If you click Decline, I only count your visit anonymously, without cookies or recordings. You can change your choice anytime with the &ldquo;Privacy choices&rdquo; link in the footer. Recordings are kept for 30 days.</p>
      <p><strong>Vercel Speed Insights.</strong> I use this to see how fast pages load for real visitors. It doesn't set cookies or collect anything that identifies you.</p>
      <p><strong>Calendly.</strong> If you book a call, Calendly handles the scheduling. It only loads when you click the booking button.</p>
      <p><strong>The email newsletter.</strong> If you sign up in the footer, Buttondown stores your email address so I can send the letter. That's the only thing it's used for. Unsubscribe anytime with the link at the bottom of any letter.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">I don't sell your data, and I don't share it beyond what these tools need to work. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:christopher@theweb3family.com">christopher@theweb3family.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+13107036003">(310) 703-6003</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
